## M&A Process

### Deal Stages

| Stage | Duration | Activities |
|-------|----------|------------|
| Sourcing | Ongoing | Target identification, outreach |
| Initial Evaluation | 2-4 weeks | Strategic fit, preliminary diligence |
| Detailed Diligence | 4-8 weeks | Full diligence, valuation |
| Negotiation | 2-4 weeks | Terms, documentation |
| Signing | 1-2 weeks | Definitive agreements |
| Closing | 4-8 weeks | Regulatory, conditions |
| Integration | 6-18 months | PMI execution |

### Due Diligence Framework

| Area | Scope | Owner |
|------|-------|-------|
| Strategic | Market, competitive, synergies | Strategy |
| Financial | Revenue, costs, projections | Finance |
| Technology | Architecture, tech debt, IP | Engineering |
| Product | Roadmap, customers, adoption | Product |
| Commercial | Sales, pipeline, retention | Sales |
| Legal | Contracts, IP, litigation | Legal |
| HR | Team, comp, culture | People |
| Security | Compliance, vulnerabilities | Security |

### Approval Authority

| Deal Size | Approval Required |
|-----------|-------------------|
| < $10M | CEO + CFO |
| $10M-$50M | Board notification |
| $50M-$100M | Board approval |
| > $100M | Board + stockholder (if equity) |

